1
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Belê temaşevanên hêja, vî carî jî me berê xwe da navçeya
Mabetan.
 
Yes dear viewers, this time we headed to the Mabeta
district.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Vê carê jî em ê derbasî du gundan bibin, du gund bûn e yek.
 
This time we will pass to two villages, two villages became
one.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Gundê Elî Cara û gundê Raca.
 
The village of Eli Caro and the village of Raco.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Dê ka em ê vê hefteyê jî em bi hev re derbas bin.
 
Let's pass through them together this week as well.

5
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Belê temaşevanên hêja, îro jî em derbasî gundê Raca û Elî
Cara bûn.
 
Yes dear viewers, today we passed to the villages of Raco
and Eli Caro.

6
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:36,000
Îro jî em derbasî du gundan bûn e. Milêtê her gunda jî li
hev kom bûn e.
 
Today we passed to two villages. The people of both villages
have gathered together.

7
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:41,000
Naha jî em li gundê Raca ne. Naha jî em ê destpêkê her
gundekî nas bikin.
 
Right now we are in the village of Raco. Now we will get to
know each village first.

8
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Merheba ji we re.
 
Hello to you.

9
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Ehlen we sehlen bi hatina we û bi zêrandina we.
 
Welcome, and thank you for visiting us.

10
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Navê min Mistefa ye, lawê Hecî 'Eme ye, ji Elî Cara.
 
My name is Mustafa, son of Haji 'Eme, from Eli Caro.

11
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Elî Cara navê xwe ji kû anî ye?
 
Where did Eli Caro get its name from?

12
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Bixwedê jaro ye. Navê lê bûye Elî, ku kirine Elî Carû. Bi
'erebî dibêjin Elî Carû, bi kurmancî jî dibêjin Elî Carê.
 
By God, he is poor. His name was Eli, which they made Eli
Jaro. In Arabic they say Eli Jaro, in Kurmanji they also say
Eli Jare.

13
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:13,000
Na, ji ber ku gundê we û Raca jî gihiştine hevdu, du gund
bûn yek, dema em derbasî gund bûn min nizanîbû kîjan gund e.
 
No, because your village and Raco have merged together, both
villages became one, when we entered the village I didn't
know which one it was.

14
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Ev Elî Cara ye an Raca ye, bi rastî an na?
 
Is this Eli Caro or Raco, right or not?

15
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Mabeyna me, Elî Cara û Raca, bes camî ye.
 
Between us, Eli Caro and Raco, is just the mosque.

16
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Haliyê camiyê yê xerbî Elî Cara ye, haliyê wê yê şerqî Raca
ye.
 
The western side of the mosque is Eli Caro, the eastern side
is Raco.

17
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:29,000
Yanî bes camî di ortê me de ye. Wekî din gundê me yek e.
 
Meaning just the mosque is between us. Otherwise our village
is one.

18
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:33,000
Niha Elî Cara, malbat yek e, an malbatên din jî hene, kesên
din jî hene?
 
Now in Eli Caro, is there one family, or are there other
families, other people?

19
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:42,000
Bixwedê malê Hesûn e, malê Hecbirîm, malê 'Eme, malê Ehmed,
malê Şêx e.
 
By God, it's the family of Hasun, Hajbirim, 'Eme, Ahmed, and
Sheikh.

20
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Evana esasê wan yek e?
 
Are their origins one?

21
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:49,000
Evana esasê wan hemû yek e. Hemû jî gundê Elî ne, gişt kurê
Elî Carê ne.
 
Their origins are all one. All are of Eli's village, all are
sons of Eli Jare.

22
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:54,000
Yanî gişt yek e, 'aîle yek e. Wekî din pismam û daîza tişt
bi wan re pê re hatin e.
 
Meaning all are one, the family is one. In addition to
cousins and other relatives that came along.

23
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,000
Dibistan jî yek e?
 
Is the school also one?

24
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:03,000
Dibistan sala 1958an da hate girtin. Kalê min mixtar bû wî
jî wî girtin da.
 
The school was opened in 1958. My grandfather was the
mukhtar, and he opened it.

25
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Sala 1958an da ku qeçkê me derin koxan da dixwendin, heta ku
mektebê me çêbû xwendin.
 
In 1958 when our kids went to read in the sheds, they
studied there until our school was built.

26
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:11,000
Pênc gundan li wê derê dixwendin, heta refa çaran.
 
Five villages studied there, up to the fourth grade.

27
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Yanî dibistan yek e, mizgeft yek e, civak yek e... Yanî hûn
hemî bi hev ra ne?
 
So the school is one, the mosque is one, the community is
one... Meaning you are all together?

28
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:22,000
Mabeyna me û Raca gişt yek e. Heta naha komîna me yek e.
 
Between us and Raco everything is one. Up until now our
commune is one.

29
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:25,000
Komîn jî yek e? Navê komîna we bi kîjan şehîdî ye?
 
The commune is also one? Which martyr is your commune named
after?

30
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:31,000
Bixwedê Şehîd Xoşnav. Navê komîna me.
 
By God, Martyr Xoshnav. The name of our commune.

31
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:32,000
Spas ji te ra jî.
 
Thank you too.

32
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:35,000
Spas ji we ra, ehlen wesehlen.
 
Thank you, you are welcome.

33
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:37,000
Merheba ji te ra jî.
 
Hello to you too.

34
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:38,000
Merheba, ehlen wesehlen bi we.
 
Hello, you are welcome.

35
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:39,000
Em te jî nas bikin destpêkê.
 
Let's get to know you first.

36
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:41,000
Elî Heme.
 
Eli Heme.

37
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,000
Ser çavên min. Tu ji Raca ye?
 
You're welcome. Are you from Raco?

38
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Bixwedê Raca me.
 
By God, I am from Raco.

39
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:50,000
Ka hinekî ji min ra li ser Raca bi axive. Ev Raca çawa çêbû
ye, navê wî ji kû hatiye?
 
Tell me a bit about Raco. How did Raco come to be, where did
its name come from?

40
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Yasîdî Raco bixwedê... lawê Çomazin e.
 
My master, Raco by God... is the son of Chomazin.

41
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:58,000
Yanî ev hatiye vir navê wî Raco bû?
 
Meaning he came here and his name was Raco?

42
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Raco bû. Raco bi xwe lawê Çomazin e.
 
It was Raco. Raco himself is the son of Chomazin.

43
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:08,000
Û qeçkê Raco çar in. Yek we re dibêjin Hem, yek jî Nas, yek
jî Henan, yek jî His.
 
And Raco's kids are four. One they call Hem, one Nas, one
Henan, and one His.

44
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:11,000
Evana qeçkê Raco ne.
 
These are Raco's kids.

45
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:20,000
Raco bi xwe lawê Çomazin e. Û hat çû, li ha fa rûnişt li ser
kaniya Rûtar rûnişt.
 
Raco himself is the son of Chomazin. He came, went, and sat
there on Rutar spring.

46
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:27,000
Jê ve jî hat dibêjin, wekî mezinê me dibêjin dibê çû li
gundê Raca rûnişt.
 
From there he came, as our elders say, he went and settled
in the village of Raco.

47
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,000
Ha vî Raco û pisê Raco.
 
This is Raco and Raco's boys.

48
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Û çar lawê wî hene?
 
And he has four sons?

49
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Çar lawê wî hene, wekî min te ra gotî: His, Henan, Hem, yek
jî Nas. Ev lawê Raco ne.
 
He has four sons, as I told you: His, Henan, Hem, and Nas.
These are Raco's sons.

50
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:40,000
Ev li kû rûniştin e?
 
Where are they settled?

51
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:48,000
Evana di gundan da ne. Hemî di gundan da ne. Bes qeçkê xwa
hene. Qeçkê qeçka hene, li vê derê.
 
They are in the villages. They are all in the villages. They
have their own kids. Their kids' kids are here.

52
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:52,000
Em bi xwe ji Heme ne. Malbatek heye ji Henan in.
 
We ourselves are from Heme. There is a family from Henan.

53
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,000
Yanî dîsa yek in.
 
Meaning you are one again.

54
00:04:53,000 --> 00:05:00,000
Giştik yek in. Em malbat gişt yek in, bes du mal di nav me
da li vir, derveyî gund da hatin e.
 
All are one. We the family are all one, only two houses
among us here, came from outside the village.

55
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:06,000
Hin dibêjin Şa'ro û mala Bekirê Reşo ji Gurda hatine vir.
 
Some are called Sha'ro and the family of Bekire Resho came
here from Gurda.

56
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:11,000
Evana ne ji Raca ne. Bes mezin bûn e, em bûn e meriv.
 
They are not from Raco. But they grew up, and we became
relatives.

57
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:13,000
Nexwe hejmara gund çiqas mal e?
 
Then what is the number of houses in the village?

58
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:17,000
Gund teqrîben 60 mal heye. Pêncî 60 mal e.
 
The village has approximately 60 houses. 50 or 60 houses.

59
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,000
Û Elî Caro?
 
And Eli Caro?

60
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:24,000
Elî Caro hew jî 30, 40 mal e. Heye 50, 60 mal in.
 
Eli Caro is also 30, 40 houses. Maybe 50, 60 houses.

61
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:27,000
Yanî gund 120, herdu gund...
 
So the village is 120, both villages...

62
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:30,000
Hesab bike 100 û 10, 100 û 20, nagîje 130 mal.
 
Count it as 110, 120, it doesn't reach 130 houses.

63
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,000
Hûn bi hev re jiyan dikin...
 
You live together...

64
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:38,000
Em gişta bi hev ra ne, di şahiya da, di miriya da... Em gişt
am bi hev ra ne.
 
We are all together, in joy, in death... We are all
together.

65
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:46,000
Komîn wekî hevalê Mistefa gotî komîna me giştik yek e, derdê
me yek e, em giştik bi hev ra ne.
 
The commune, as my friend Mustafa said, our commune is one,
our pain is one, we are all together.

66
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:50,000
Mala we ava be. Em îna derbasî cem yê din jî bibin.
 
God bless you. We will now pass to the others as well.

67
00:05:50,000 --> 00:06:10,000
Ser seran spas ji te ra jî, ehlen wesehlen...
 
You are most welcome, thank you too...

68
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:18,000
Gundê Elî Caro û Raca girêdayî navçeya Mabetan e. Nêzî 15
kîlometrî li rojavayê Mabeta dikevin.
 
The villages of Eli Caro and Raco belong to the Mabeta
district. They are located nearly 15 kilometers west of
Mabeta.

69
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:23,000
Gundê Elî Caro û gundê Raca bûn e yek gund, û malên wan
gihîştin e hevdu.
 
The village of Eli Caro and the village of Raco have become
one village, and their houses have merged.

70
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:26,000
Goristan, dibistan û komîna wan yek e.
 
Their cemetery, school, and commune are one.

71
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:35,000
Gundê Elî Caro û Raca, li ser çiyayekî bi navê Çiyayê Gêza,
zêra hatin e avakirin. Û di nav herêmek çiyayî da ne.
 
The villages of Eli Caro and Raco were built on a mountain
called the Geza Zera Mountain. And they are in a mountainous
region.

72
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:38,000
Ev çiya bi darên zeytûnan xemilandî ne.
 
These mountains are adorned with olive trees.

73
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:47,000
Her wek tê gotin, ku di demên borî da hemû daristanên mûrxê
bûn, û ta naha hinek daristan li derdora gund hene.
 
As it is said, in the past they were all pine forests, and
even now there are some forests around the village.

74
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:51,000
Û hawîrdorê bi şînahiyê dixemilînin.
 
And they decorate the surroundings with greenery.

75
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:57,000
Navê gundê Elî Caro ji navê kesekî bi navê Elîyê Carê
hatiye.
 
The name of the village of Eli Caro comes from the name of a
person called Eliye Jare.

76
00:06:57,000 --> 00:07:01,000
Ji Elîyê Carê tê der û ji wî çar kur çêdibin.
 
He originates from Eliye Jare, and he had four sons.

77
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:08,000
Hecbirîm, Os, Ehmed û Şêx e. Û bi vî awayî gund mezin dibe,
û koka wan ji êla Biyan e.
 
Hajbirim, Os, Ahmed, and Sheikh. And this way the village
grows, and their origin is from the Biyan tribe.

78
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:14,000
Gundê Elî Caro ji 60 xanî pêk tê, û nêzî 500 kes lê dijîn.
 
The village of Eli Caro consists of 60 houses, and nearly
500 people live there.

79
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:22,000
Navê gundê Raca ji kesekî bi navê Recê Çomazin hatiye. Ku ev
wek damezrînerê gund tê naskirin.
 
The name of the village of Raco comes from a person called
Reje Chomazin. He is known as the founder of the village.

80
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:26,000
An ku kesê yekemîn li gund niştecî bû ye.
 
Or the first person to settle in the village.

81
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:36,000
Tê gotin ku sê kurên Çomazin hebûn, yek ji wan bi navê Rece
li vir ma, yê din jî çû li gundê Sewliyê li navçeya Atme
niştecî bû.
 
It is said that Chomazin had three sons, one of them named
Rece stayed here, and the other went and settled in the
village of Sawliye in the Atme district.

82
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:39,000
Û naha ew malbata Kurdî têne naskirin.
 
And now they are known as a Kurdish family.

83
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:48,000
Û yê sêyemîn bi navê Heme Rece li deverek nêzî Raco niştecî
bû ye û nav lê bûye gundê Rajo.
 
And the third, named Heme Rece, settled in a place near
Raco, and it was named the village of Rajo.

84
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:54,000
Sê malbatên bingehîn di gundê Raca da hene. Osê, Heme Rece,
û malbata Wahîd.
 
There are three main families in the village of Raco. Ose,
Heme Rece, and the Wahid family.

85
00:07:54,000 --> 00:08:12,000
An ku bi giştî derdora nod xanî û nêzî 1100 kes li herdû
gundan dijîn, û herdû gund mîna gundekî ne.
 
In total, around 90 houses and nearly 1100 people live in
both villages, and both villages are like one village.

86
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:18,000
Belê temaşevanên hêja, di gundê Elî Caro da jî, em derbasî
cem mixtêr bûn. Cem apê Remzî.
 
Yes dear viewers, in the village of Eli Caro as well, we
went to the mukhtar. With uncle Ramzi.

87
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:24,000
Naha em ê bi hevre Apê Remzî jî nas bikin. Apê Remzî jî
leşkeriya Fransa kiriye.
 
Now we will get to know uncle Ramzi together. Uncle Ramzi
also did military service for France.

88
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:25,000
Merheba ji te ra.
 
Hello to you.

89
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,000
Ehlen wesehlen.
 
Welcome.

90
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:30,000
Apê Remzî, emrê te çiqas sal e?
 
Uncle Ramzi, how old are you?

91
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:35,000
Welleh nizanim, ez di ser heştê ra me. Heştê nizanim tişt...
 
By God I don't know, I'm over eighty. Eighty I don't know
something...

92
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:41,000
Dema tu bûyî leşker, te eskeriya Fransa kir, tê bîra te tu
di kîjan salê da bû?
 
When you became a soldier, you did military service for
France, do you remember what year you were in?

93
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:47,000
Erê. Demek amrê min 18, 17 bû, ez ji Tirkiyê revîm hatim...
 
Yes. When my age was 18, 17, I fled from Turkey and came...

94
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:54,000
Bûm eskerê Fransayê û min çar salan jî eskerîya Firansayê
kir.
 
I became a soldier for France and I did military service for
France for four years.

95
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:57,000
Tu li kû derê bû? Li bakur? Te li nêzîk kir?
 
Where were you? In the north? Did you do it nearby?

96
00:08:57,000 --> 00:09:08,000
Li vê derê... li Efrînê... li Ezzazê... minteqeya Ezzazê,
heta Çobambegê... heta Cerablusê. Min li wê minteqeyê eskerî
kir.
 
Here... in Afrin... in Azaz... the Azaz region, up to
Cobanbey... up to Jarablus. I did military service in that
region.

97
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:12,000
Yanî tê bîra te, tu di kîjan wextê da bû, di kîjan salê da
bû?
 
Meaning do you remember what time it was, what year it was
in?

98
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:25,000
Ey derê. Kî li bîra xwe digre tu salan dipirse û tu asasan
dipirse. Herkesek îro bi kîfê xwe ye, ne?
 
Oh man. Who remembers, you're asking about years and you're
asking about specifics. Everyone is on their own today,
right?

99
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,000
Te çar salan eskerî kir?
 
You did military service for four years?

100
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:30,000
Çar salan min cîb Firansa eskerî kir.
 
I did military service for France for four years in a jeep.

101
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:35,000
Hevalên te wê demê kî bûn, kesek ji menqiteqê we, ji gundê
we hebû?
 
Who were your friends at that time, was there anyone from
your region, from your village?

102
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:42,000
Hevalên min ji minteqeya me tune ne.
 
I had no friends from our region.

103
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:43,000
Ji kû derê hebûn?
 
Where were they from?

104
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:48,000
Ji minteqeya Bilbilê hebûn.
 
They were from the Bilbil region.

105
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:58,000
Wekî din tu bera xwe bidî xêlê, bi giştî min kesekî ji
Firansa re eskerî nekir.
 
Otherwise, if you look at this tribe in general, none of my
people did military service for France.

106
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:00,000
E wê demê leşkerî...
 
And military service at that time...

107
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:05,000
Dema, Kurmancên me pir bûn di leşkeriya tiştê avakirî,
Fransayê kirî?
 
Back then, were there many of our Kurmancis in the army that
France established?

108
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:13,000
Kurmanc, Kurmancî... dîmek, eskaderonek hebû, jê ra digotin
eskaderona Kurd.
 
Kurmanc, Kurmanci... I mean, there was a squadron, they
called it the Kurdish squadron.

109
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:23,000
Lêcê, nav lê nan, wextê ku herbê çolaq rabû, Fransayê herbê
çolaq rabû.
 
The Legion, they named it, when the battle of Çolaq broke
out, France started the battle of Çolaq.

110
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:26,000
Çolaq neşkandin, nekuştin.
 
They didn't defeat Çolaq, they didn't kill him.

111
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:35,000
Çolaq kuştin, rabûn kirin Eskaderona Lêcê Kurd, l'exê.
 
They killed Çolaq, they went and made the Kurdish Squadron
of the Legion, the legion.

112
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:44,000
Yanî Kurmanc li miraza xwe xistin, heta ba Fransayê, ba ewa
kir.
 
I mean the Kurmancis got what they wanted, even with France,
with them.

113
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:54,000
Yanî negotin çolaq, Kurmanca kuştin, gotin eskaderona Kurd
Lêcê, l'exê.
 
I mean they didn't say Kurmancis killed Çolaq, they said the
Kurdish Squadron of the Legion, the legion.

114
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:56,000
Yanî tê çi wateyê da?
 
So what does that mean?

115
00:10:56,000 --> 00:11:00,000
Yanî wateya wê ewe ku, Kurmanc li miraza xwe xistin.
 
Its meaning is that, Kurmancis achieved their goal.

116
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:06,000
Kurmanc li miraza xwe xistin bi çûcanê.
 
Kurmancis achieved their goal through fighting (bravery).

117
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:14,000
Ewa mişteşarî Fransa, ev l'exeb e da ewan, kurmanca.
 
That French advisor gave this title to them, the Kurmancis.

118
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:17,000
Dema, ev şerê bi ye diji çolaq te bîra te?
 
Back then, do you remember this war against Çolaq?

119
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:25,000
Nayê bîra min bes wekî çîrokê gotin mezinên me, ha.
 
I don't remember it but like a story our elders told us,
yes.

120
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:33,000
Û wextê çolaq ku herbê bike, hat, da bavê min ji derbaz bû.
 
And when Çolaq came to wage war, he came, then my father
also passed by.

121
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:37,000
Dîmek bavê min ji vir bû, çolaq ji berra derbaz bû.
 
I mean my father was from here, Çolaq passed from below him.

122
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:42,000
Çolaq, çil, wî mir... xelkê, Çeqel omer...
 
Çolaq, forty, he died... people, Çeqel Omer...

123
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:44,000
Li wir derê kuştin.
 
They killed him there.

124
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:50,000
Ewe dema da çolaq bi uh Mehmed Dînê Îbşoşê bû, ew dema da li
hember Fransa şer kir?
 
At that time, was Çolaq with, uh, Mehmed Dînê Îbşoşê, at
that time did he fight against France?

125
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:55,000
Na na na, Mehmed Dînê Îbşoşê, berya wî, berya wî bû...
 
No no no, Mehmed Dînê Îbşoşê was before him, before him...

126
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:56,000
Berya çolaq...
 
Before Çolaq...

127
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:58,000
Berya çolaq.
 
Before Çolaq.

128
00:11:58,000 --> 00:11:59,000
Mehmed Dînê Îbşoşê.
 
Mehmed Dînê Îbşoşê.

129
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:00,000
Wî ji li hember Fransa şer kir?
 
Did he also fight against France?

130
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:02,000
Wî ji kir, Mehmed Dînê Îbşoşê ji kir.
 
He did too, Mehmed Dînê Îbşoşê did too.

131
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:06,000
Yanî yê destpêkê şer li hember Fransa kirî Mehmed Dînê
Îbşoşê bû.
 
So the one who first fought against France was Mehmed Dînê
Îbşoşê.

132
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:18,000
Ê. Paşê çolaq kir, çolaq dîmek da ewa da de.. de gundê
kêmraşê da, de girê ewa da mir.
 
Yes. Then Çolaq did, Çolaq I mean in that... in the village
of Kêmraş, in that hill he died.

133
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:20,000
Piştî wî ti bûyî eskerê Fransa?
 
After him you became a French soldier?

134
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:22,000
Piştî wî em bûn eskerê Fransa.
 
After him we became French soldiers.

135
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:26,000
Dîmek Evdo kurakê xwe bû.
 
I mean Evdo was his boy.

136
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:28,000
Kurakê Çolaq bû.
 
He was Çolaq's boy.

137
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:35,000
Evdo kuştin, paşê ew kuştin, paşê çolaq kuştin, lê...
 
They killed Evdo, then they killed him, then they killed
Çolaq, but...

138
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:37,000
Eskerê xwe pir bûn?
 
Were his soldiers many?

139
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:48,000
Dîmek wê çaxê eskerê Kurmanc, teyin kirin ji qereqola hatin,
l'çolaq xistin. Ji paşva hatin.
 
I mean at that time the Kurmanci soldiers, they appointed
them, they came from the outposts, they hit Çolaq. They came
from behind.

140
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:50,000
Ewe dema da ji qereqolê hatin...
 
At that time they came from the outpost...

141
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:53,000
Ji qereqolê hatin.
 
They came from the outpost.

142
00:12:53,000 --> 00:13:00,000
Dîmek wê çaxê Fransa, eskerê xwe, eskaderonek pêra
digotin...
 
I mean at that time France, its soldiers, they called a
squadron with them...

143
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:04,000
Çi pêra dibêjin jê...
 
What do they call it...

144
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:09,000
Dîmek sed eskerê wê çaxê.
 
I mean a hundred soldiers at that time.

145
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:15,000
Wê çaxê ji paşva hatin li çolaq xistin.
 
At that time they came from behind and hit Çolaq.

146
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:22,000
Ji evê da hatin, ji încirniyê da hilkişîn.
 
They came from here, they climbed up from Incirni.

147
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:31,000
Hatin, çolaq ji wê, dûziyê. Ji paşva hatin li çolaq xistin,
çolaq kuştin.
 
They came, Çolaq was from there, the plain. They came from
behind and hit Çolaq, they killed Çolaq.

148
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:33,000
Ê çi te bîrate hîne divê deman da, çi tişt hebûn?
 
So what else do you remember from those times, what things
were there?

149
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:43,000
Dîmek wê çaxê, hîne, yanî emrê min di deh û sê, deh û çar,
deh û pênc, hene di van...
 
I mean at that time, still, I mean my age was around
thirteen, fourteen, fifteen, somewhere in these...

150
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:46,000
Yanî di sêzdeh salî, panzdeh salî ewe demê te bîra te..
 
I mean around thirteen years old, fifteen years old that
time you remember..

151
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:49,000
Ê we çaxê tê bîra min.
 
Yes, that time I remember.

152
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:59,000
Apê Remzî te divê dema te got der efrînê da te çuyê
cerablûsê ji divê demê da. Wê şer li hember kesekê kir. te
şerek kir yan na?
 
Uncle Remzi, in that time you said you went outside Afrin to
Cerablus too in that time. There you fought against someone.
Did you fight or not?

153
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:02,000
Na em ti şer nekir, min di mexfere da bû.
 
No we didn't do any fighting, I was in the outpost.

154
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:03,000
Tu weke mexfere dabû?
 
You were in the outpost?

155
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:10,000
L'mexfere, işte teyîn dikir tikare, mesele çobanbeg tikare
cerablusê tikare wê..
 
In the outpost, well they appointed you anywhere, for
example Çobanbey, anywhere Cerablus, anywhere there..

156
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:13,000
Fransa hawa teyin ji, Fransa diçe di...
 
France appointed like this, France goes in...

157
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:19,000
Fransa demek dirêj li vir ma. Te bîrate dema jivir derketî
te çûyî, a?
 
France stayed here for a long time. Do you remember when
they left here and went, huh?

158
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:33,000
Wextê ji vir derketin? Wextê ji vir derketin em te ra
bibêjim dema ko li cerablusê bûn.
 
When they left here? When they left here let me tell you,
when we were in Cerablus.

159
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:41,000
Dema Fransa ji vir çûya, de çil û şeşa da ji vir çû, divê
dema da kî, kî li hemberê şer kir?
 
When France left here, they left here in '46, at that time
who, who fought against them?

160
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:45,000
Kurmanca mekir. Qa na ereba kir.
 
Kurmancis didn't do it. But Arabs did.

161
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:46,000
Kurda li hember Fransa şernekirin?
 
Kurds didn't fight against France?

162
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:49,000
Ne, Kurda kir...Kî bûn divê dema da?
 
No, Kurds did... Who were they at that time?

163
00:14:49,000 --> 00:15:01,000
Dîmek wê çaxê işte Reşîd Îbo hebû, Mehe Îbşoşê, berî wê,
Mehe Îbşoşê berî Çolaq..
 
I mean at that time there was Reşid Ibo, Mehe Ibşoşê, before
that, Mehe Ibşoşê before Çolaq..

164
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:13,000
Paşê Çolaq hat, paşê işte te ra hatin Kurmanc, dîmek Mehe
Îbşoşê ji berî Çolaq e. Neye di berî e, berî, berye.
 
Then Çolaq came, then Kurmancis came to you, I mean Mehe
Ibşoşê is before Çolaq. He's not before, before, before.

165
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:22,000
Na ev eskerê Fransa, di çiyayê Kurmênc da te nizane kî û kî
nene, te navên nas dikî, kî bûn?
 
No, these French soldiers, in Kurd Dagh, don't you know
who's who, you know names, who were they?

166
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:26,000
Kî, her yek, her navçe ji şiyê hebûn, ji bilbilê hebûn. Her
navçeyê henek hebûn.
 
Who, everyone, every district, there were some from Şiyê,
there were some from Bilbilê. Every district had some.

167
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:27,000
Ji Şiyê hebûn.
 
There were from Şiyê.

168
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:32,000
Ji qitmê hebûn e ekseriyet ji qitmê, ji qirqilaxê mezin.
 
There were from Qitmê, the majority were from Qitmê, from
the big Qirqilax.

169
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:46,000
Ekseriyet ji qirqilaxê mezin. U ji qitmê hebûn. Ehmed Şêxo
bû ji qitmê, ehmed şêxo, erê...ji quqilaxê mezin, ew bû.
Ehmed şêxo bû.
 
The majority were from the big Qirqilax. And there were from
Qitmê. Ahmed Shexo was from Qitmê, Ahmed Shexo, yes... from
the big Qirqilax, it was him. Ahmed Shexo was.

170
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:51,000
Biraq hebû bedrî, biraq jî hebû.
 
Biraq was there, Bedri, Biraq was there too.

171
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:53,000
Apê remzî ti çax bûyî mixtar?
 
Uncle Remzi, when did you become mukhtar?

172
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:59,000
Ez ji roja hafeze esed, gel çêkir û avakirî..
 
I am since the day Hafez Al-Assad, made and built the
people...

173
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:00,000
Te de destpêk kirî?
 
Did you start then?

174
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:05,000
Yanî çil û pênc sal e. Çil û pênc sale.
 
I mean it's been forty-five years. It's been forty-five
years.

175
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,000
Te mixtarê şeş gundaye?
 
Are you the mukhtar of six villages?

176
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:21,000
Erê, Hezecê ye yek. Mehserkê yê du, Birka se, sê, reşa..
 
Yes, Hezecê is one. Mehserkê is two, Birka is three, Reşa..

177
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:22,000
Çar.
 
Four.

178
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:30,000
Mistheşuraye pênc. Çomezna şeş gundin. Şeş gundana.
 
Mistheshura is five. Chomezna are six villages. Six
villages.

179
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:34,000
Tu mixtarê şeş gundaye, û heta niha ti mixtare. Erê.
 
You are the mukhtar of six villages, and you're still a
mukhtar till now. Yes.

180
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:40,000
Serkeftin jtera, e mixtar dema ti bûyî mixtar hîn nah navên
gundê we jî hatin guherîn.
 
Success to you. Well mukhtar, when you became a mukhtar,
even now your village names were changed.

181
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:44,000
Yanî wê demê dewleta Sûriyê ji gehurin navê, ev navê çebun
e?
 
I mean at that time the Syrian state changed the names too,
what did these names become?

182
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:56,000
E, Sûriyê gawurîn.. Navê, yanî gawurandina xwe mesele El-
Hîcarû. El-Hîcarû. Eses e...Eses e gundê.
 
Yes, Syria changed them.. The name, I mean their change for
example El-Hijaru. El-Hijaru. It's the base... it's the base
of the village.

183
00:16:56,000 --> 00:17:07,000
Şorê turkî jê ra xistin... e tirkî...mesele gundin hene
mehsercik..
 
They put Turkish talk on it... ah Turkish... for example
there are villages like Mehsercik..

184
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:10,000
Mehsera lê kirin...
 
They made it Mehsera...

185
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:13,000
Cik ra kirin.
 
They removed the 'cik'.

186
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:28,000
Ê gundên me hemî çar cara navbûn, destpêkê xwe kurmancî bûn,
piştî wê Roman hat Aramiya da, dîsa nav gaweherîn. Tirk
hatin dîsa gawurî. Sûrî hat dîsa gawurî. Bes gund weke bere
mane wek nav wek bere mane yanî.
 
Ah our villages all were named four times, at first they
were Kurmanci, after that Romans came in Aramaic, they
changed names again. Turks came, changed again. Syria came,
changed again. But the village remained as before, like the
name, remained as before I mean.

187
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:29,000
Wek bere man..
 
Remained as before.

188
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:34,000
Her demê henek hat, navê gundê me gawurîn. Erê.
 
Every time some came, they changed the names of our
villages. Yes.

189
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:37,000
Mala te ava be, spas jtera.
 
May your home prosper, thanks to you.

190
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:39,000
Ehle û sehle, mît sele.
 
Welcome, a hundred welcomes.

191
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:48,000
Ser çava.
 
You're welcome.

192
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:51,000
Her du gundên nava têkelî û peywendîyên baş dane.
 
Both villages named, they have good relations and
connections.

193
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:57,000
Di aheng şahî û xemgînîyê de bi hevdû ra alîkar in, û
desteka didin hevdû.
 
In celebrations, weddings and sorrows, they help each other,
and they support each other.

194
00:17:57,000 --> 00:18:04,000
Xelkên her du gundan debara xwe bi çandiniyê dikin, mîna
hemî gundên navçeyê.
 
The people of both villages make their living from
agriculture, like all the villages in the district.

195
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:24,000
Darên zeytûnê berhemên sereke ne. Ligel zeytûnan darên fêkî
jî tên çandin.
 
Olive trees are the main products. Along with olives, fruit
trees are also planted.

196
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:42,000
Mesele merheba jtera.
 
Well, hello to you.

197
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:44,000
Merhaba jtera jê. Ehle û sehlen.
 
Hello to you too. Welcome.

198
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:46,000
Spas jtera em destpêkê te nasbikin.
 
Thank you, let's first get to know you.

199
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:48,000
Edhem...
 
Edhem...

200
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:49,000
Êê..
 
Yes..

201
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:50,000
Jî Elî Caro.
 
From Ali Caro.

202
00:18:50,000 --> 00:19:03,000
Spas jtera ji.. Ser çavê min. Naha ev ciyê em lê, ev geliyê,
bi navê bîrê tê naskirin. Wekî te behs kirîye. Ev bîra, çend
gund li ser av dibirin? Çend gunda av ji vê bîrê dibir yanî?
 
Thank you too.. You're welcome. Now this place we are in,
this valley, is known by the name of the well. As you
mentioned. This well, how many villages took water from it?
How many villages took water from this well, I mean?

203
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:07,000
Vê bîrê, bîrê..heft gunda debir.. bere..
 
This well, the well... seven villages used to take from
it... in the past..

204
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:14,000
Heft gund da dihatin dibirin.. Mehserkê, Birka, Çumezna,
Raco.
 
Seven villages used to come and take... Mehserkê, Birka,
Çumezna, Raco.

205
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:18,000
Mistheşura, hec qasim û gişk berê dihatin av ji vê bîrê
dibirin.
 
Mistheshura, Hec Qasim and all of them used to come and take
water from this well.

206
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:22,000
Av berê tune bû. Bes naha gundekî av çêbûye her kes bi ava
xwe deçe.
 
There was no water before. But now in every village water
has been made, everyone goes with their own water.

207
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:25,000
Vê bîrê ji ha wa mahcûr mane ko..
 
This well is left abandoned like this..

208
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:27,000
Mesele salek we da, tekra me hecer lê miş kir.
 
For example a year like that, again we built stones on it.

209
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:30,000
Manê l'hênî bîrek eseri ye, kevn e.
 
Meaning it's still a historical well, it's old.

210
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:32,000
E weke kûmîn?
 
Ah like a commune?

211
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:34,000
Um, kumîn e, me çêkir.
 
Yes, commune, we built it.

212
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:38,000
Kumînê gund me ew kir, me çêkir, me hazir kir.
 
The village commune we did it, we built it, we prepared it.

213
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:42,000
Naha ev gundên te behsê kirî, naha beg, Mistheşura l'kû derê
dikevin? Ev gundana.
 
Now these villages you mentioned, now sir, where is
Mistheşura located? These villages.

214
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:47,000
Jiber ku dema em derbaz gundê we bûn, e, Musteşur li vir ne
xuya bû... di milî din de dikeve?
 
Because when we passed by your village, ah, Musteşur wasn't
visible here... is it on the other side?

215
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:51,000
Mistheşura hew j'vira nêzîk e, l'vira di geliyê ra nêzîk e
dihatin vir.
 
Mistheshura is close to here, they used to come here from
the valley nearby.

216
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:54,000
Bi dewar dihatin, av dibirin.
 
They used to come with cattle, they took water.

217
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:57,000
O ev geliyê jî hamî bi vê bîrê tê naskirin.
 
And this valley is also entirely known by this well.

218
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:58,000
B'hamî b'vê bîrê tê naskirin.
 
It is entirely known by this well.

219
00:19:58,000 --> 00:19:59,000
Geliyê bîrê.
 
The well's valley.

220
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Ey.
 
Yes.

221
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:01,000
Bira, kêfa we ne?
 
Brother, are you having a good time?

222
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:06,000
Na bira, welleh jê...
 
No brother, by God from...

